    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "*** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW ***  CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** CANCELLED OPEN VIEW *** \r\n\r\nSuperbly positioned within this highly sought-after residential development, 5 Dun Oir Avenue is an exceptional double fronted, three-bedroom, A rated, semi-detached family home, presented in showhouse condition throughout. Enjoying a wonderfully bright interior and a private rear garden, the home occupies a convenient setting just off the Enniskerry Road in Kilternan, Dublin 18.\r\n\r\nThe beautifully appointed accommodation is both spacious and light filled, extending to an entrance hall with excellent storage and a guest wc. The dual aspect living room is particularly inviting, with double doors opening directly onto the rear garden, while the equally bright dual aspect kitchen / dining room provides an excellent setting for everyday family living and entertaining. A separate utility room offers additional practicality.\r\n\r\nAt first floor level, the landing incorporates a generous storage closet together with Stira access to the large attic, which, once floored, would provide excellent additional storage. There are three well-proportioned bedrooms, comprising two generous doubles, including the principal bedroom with en suite shower room, and a spacious single bedroom. A well-appointed family bathroom completes the accommodation.\r\n\r\nTo the front, the property is benefits from two designated private parking spaces, with attractive, colourful planting that creates a welcoming first impression. Additional visitor parking is conveniently positioned to the side of the development, together with electric vehicle charging points. A gated side passage leads through to the private rear garden, which is laid out in lawn and patio, and enhanced by an appealing selection planting. A secure steel garden shed provides excellent additional storage, while the garden itself offers an ideal setting for children to play, as well as for outdoor dining and entertaining.\r\n\r\nNestled at the foothills of the Dublin Mountains, Dun Oir enjoys an enviable location within easy reach of Stepaside Village, with its excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and everyday amenities. The area is exceptionally well served for recreation and leisure, with Fernhill Park and Gardens, Dundrum Town Centre, Sandyford Business Park, Beacon South Quarter, Leopardstown Racecourse and Westwood Club all within convenient reach. Numerous golf clubs and equestrian centres are also close by, while the surrounding Dublin Mountains provide an abundance of scenic walking and mountain biking routes.\r\n\r\nFamilies are particularly well catered for, with an excellent choice of primary and secondary schools in the locality, including Our Lady of the Wayside National School, Gaelscoil Thaobh na Coille, Kilternan Church of Ireland National School, Stepaside Educate Together and Rosemont School.\r\n\r\nTransport links are equally impressive, with convenient access to the LUAS Green Line together with Dublin Bus routes 44, L26 and 27. The M50 and N11 are also readily accessible, providing excellent connectivity to Dublin city centre and the wider surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nCombining beautifully presented accommodation, excellent energy efficiency, a superb location and an attractive private rear garden, 5 Dun Oir Avenue is a most appealing family home that is sure to attract strong interest from a wide variety of discerning purchasers."
      },
